   "title": "Question 9 · Extras · The tail formula · Practice 03 Q1 / Tutorial 5 Q3",
   "difficulty": "advanced",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "(a) $X\\ge0$ is continuous with CDF $F_X$. Show that $E[X]=\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\infty}\\big(1-F_X(t)\\big)\\,dt$ (assume $t\\,(1-F_X(t))\\to0$ as $t\\to\\infty$). Use it to find the mean of an exponential. (b) Use the whole-number version $E[N]=\\sum_{k\\ge0}P(N>k)$ to find the mean of a Geometric$(p)$ on $k=1,2,\\dots$",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **By parts:** $u=1-F_X(t)$, $dv=dt$, so $du=-f_X(t)\\,dt$ and $v=t$.",
     "latex": "\\int_0^{\\infty}(1-F_X(t))\\,dt=\\Big[t\\,(1-F_X(t))\\Big]_0^{\\infty}+\\int_0^{\\infty}t\\,f_X(t)\\,dt"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "The bracket is $0$ at both ends.",
     "latex": "=0+E[X]"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Exponential:** $1-F_X(t)=e^{-\\lambda t}$.",
     "latex": "E[X]=\\int_0^{\\infty}e^{-\\lambda t}\\,dt=\\frac1\\lambda"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "If $X$ can be negative (Tutorial 5 Q3), the same by-parts on $(-\\infty,0]$ subtracts one more piece.",
     "latex": "E[X]=\\int_0^{\\infty}(1-F_X)\\,dt-\\int_{-\\infty}^{0}F_X\\,dt"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) $N>k$ means the first $k$ tries failed. Geometric series.",
     "latex": "E[N]=\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty}(1-p)^k=\\frac{1}{1-(1-p)}=\\frac1p"
    }
   ],
